\pard\sa220\b\fs35\cf1 HLD: Request Management Platform\cf0\b0\par
\pard\sa130\fs18\i Author: Sergei Budnik | Public educational adaptation (2026) | Source: HIGH _LEVEL_ARCITECTURE_EXAMPLE_1.docx\i0\par
\pard\sa180\fs18 This is an anonymized, editable Word-compatible public edition. The full private source, company identifiers, production deployment parameters and embedded original diagrams are not reproduced.\par
\pard\sb240\sa100\b\fs25\cf1 1. Business context and use cases\cf0\b0\par
\pard\sa120\fs20 Request-management system for creating, editing, reviewing, assigning, rejecting, revising, archiving and closing application requests. Original HLD contained separate use-case, context, component and container diagrams.\par
\pard\li300\fi-170\sa80\fs19 - Business requester: create/edit application and search/view records.\par
\pard\li300\fi-170\sa80\fs19 - Data manager: search, review, approve or return an application and assign to a specialist.\par
\pard\li300\fi-170\sa80\fs19 - Business partner: coordinate and approve submitted applications.\par
\pard\li300\fi-170\sa80\fs19 - Data engineer: take assigned work, process or return a request and close the activity.\par
\pard\li300\fi-170\sa80\fs19 - Metrics and automated email notifications are supporting processes.\par
\pard\sb240\sa100\b\fs25\cf1 2. Context and security boundaries\cf0\b0\par
\pard\sa120\fs20 User workstations connect to a browser portal via authenticated HTTPS. The ingress boundary forwards frontend and API calls to controlled backend services. A separate permissions service, notification provider and data store are supporting components. The source referenced a corporate identity service and monitoring platform; the public edition omits their proper names.\par
\pard\li300\fi-170\sa80\fs19 - Human roles: requester, manager, business partner, data engineer.\par
\pard\li300\fi-170\sa80\fs19 - External dependencies: identity source, email provider, centralized audit/monitoring.\par
\pard\li300\fi-170\sa80\fs19 - Data ownership: request service owns application lifecycle; authorization service owns access decisions.\par
\pard\li300\fi-170\sa80\fs19 - Editable context, components and container diagrams: static/editable/requests-architecture.drawio.\par
\pard\sb240\sa100\b\fs25\cf1 3. Logical component catalogue\cf0\b0\par
\pard\sa85\b\fs18 Component\tab Responsibility\tab Technology\b0\par
\pard\li120\sa90\fs18 Request Portal\tab Create/edit, search and view application requests\tab ReactJS\par
\pard\li120\sa90\fs18 API Gateway\tab Authentication context, routing, common request checks\tab Java / Spring Cloud Gateway\par
\pard\li120\sa90\fs18 Request Management Service\tab Business lifecycle for applications and assignments\tab Java / Spring Boot\par
\pard\li120\sa90\fs18 Authorization Service\tab Access model, role and operation permissions\tab Java / Spring Boot\par
\pard\li120\sa90\fs18 Notification Service\tab Prepare and send application-change notifications\tab Java / Spring Boot\par
\pard\sb240\sa100\b\fs25\cf1 4. External interactions (source structure 1.x)\cf0\b0\par
\pard\sa85\b\fs18 ID\tab Initiator to recipient\tab Purpose / protocol\b0\par
\pard\li120\sa90\fs18 1.9\tab Notification component to mail provider\tab Email notifications; SMTP\par
\pard\li120\sa90\fs18 1.11\tab Business requester to portal\tab Create/edit/search/view; HTTPS sync\par
\pard\li120\sa90\fs18 1.12\tab Data manager to portal\tab Review and assign; HTTPS sync\par
\pard\li120\sa90\fs18 1.13\tab Business partner to portal\tab Coordinate/approve; HTTPS sync\par
\pard\li120\sa90\fs18 1.14\tab Data engineer to portal\tab Take/fulfil tasks; HTTPS sync\par
\pard\li120\sa90\fs18 1.15\tab Monitoring to platform\tab Request health/metrics; HTTPS sync\par
\pard\sb240\sa100\b\fs25\cf1 5. Internal interactions (source structure 2.x)\cf0\b0\par
\pard\sa85\b\fs18 ID\tab Source to target\tab Purpose / interface\b0\par
\pard\li120\sa90\fs18 2.1\tab Authenticated user to ingress\tab HTTPS client ingress\par
\pard\li120\sa90\fs18 2.2\tab Ingress to web frontend\tab Serve frontend resources\par
\pard\li120\sa90\fs18 2.4\tab Domain services to database cluster\tab Transactional data access over secured DB channel\par
\pard\li120\sa90\fs18 2.5\tab Ingress to API Gateway\tab Route API commands\par
\pard\li120\sa90\fs18 2.6\tab API Gateway to Request Service\tab Create / edit / search request\par
\pard\li120\sa90\fs18 2.7\tab Service layer to monitoring\tab Metrics and auditable events\par
\pard\li120\sa90\fs18 2.8\tab Gateway to Authorization Service\tab Fetch caller permissions\par
\pard\li120\sa90\fs18 2.9\tab Request/notification services to Authorization\tab Check operation permission\par
\pard\li120\sa90\fs18 2.10\tab Request Service to Notification Service\tab Prepare notification\par
\pard\li120\sa90\fs18 2.11\tab Services to centralized audit system\tab Submit audit information\par
\pard\sb240\sa100\b\fs25\cf1 6. Design review and decisions\cf0\b0\par
\pard\li300\fi-170\sa80\fs19 - Clarify service ownership of application status, concurrency and immutable audit.\par
\pard\li300\fi-170\sa80\fs19 - Enforce role-based authorization on server rather than UI only.\par
\pard\li300\fi-170\sa80\fs19 - Classify notification failure independently from application approval outcome.\par
\pard\li300\fi-170\sa80\fs19 - Define request idempotency, duplicate prevention, timeout and recovery contracts.\par
\pard\li300\fi-170\sa80\fs19 - Record real SLO targets, network access, encryption and data retention before production.\par
\pard\sb240\sa100\b\fs25\cf1 7. Linked editable diagrams\cf0\b0\par
